{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a8cc30b2-9260-4ea9-b7d5-f1544e53cf9d",
    "name": "LEGLINK-580 Inactive Code Validation",
    "description": "End-to-end check that an inactive code surfaces as a validation Result and categorizes as a `missing_active_*` category.\n\nRun the requests top-to-bottom. Set the collection variables first (Variables tab):\n- `validationBaseUrl` (local: http://localhost:8075)\n- `terminologyBaseUrl` (local: http://localhost:8076)\n- `codeSystem`, `code`, `codeDisplay` — an INACTIVE code known to the terminology service\n- `codeSystemId` — the terminology CodeSystem id used by the config lookup endpoint\n- `resourceType` / `profileUrl` / `bindingValueSetUrl` — the resource, profile, and bound value set the code sits on (drives the sample bundle)\n\nPrereqs for LOCAL: validation must be wired to the terminology service (App Config is disabled locally). Add a docker-compose.override.yml:\n\n  services:\n    validation:\n      environment:\n        link.terminology-service-url: http://terminology:8076\n\nThe test env already has `link.terminology-service-url` set via Azure App Config, so there you only need requests 5-9.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "55093274"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health - Validation",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Validation service is up', () => pm.response.code < 500);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{validationBaseUrl}}/health",
          "host": [
            "{{validationBaseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "health"
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Health - Terminology",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Terminology service is up', () => pm.response.code < 500);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}/health",
          "host": [
            "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "health"
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Terminology - Reload Cache",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Cache reload accepted', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 202, 204]));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}/api/terminology/config/$reload-cache",
          "host": [
            "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "terminology",
            "config",
            "$reload-cache"
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "3b. Terminology - List loaded CodeSystems (discover ids)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "const entries = b.entry || [];",
              "console.log('Loaded CodeSystems (' + entries.length + '):');",
              "entries.forEach(e => { const cs = e.resource || {}; console.log(`  id=${cs.id}  url=${cs.url}  version=${cs.version}`); });",
              "console.log('Set collection vars codeSystemId=<id> and codeSystem=<url> from a row above, then pick an inactive code for that system.');",
              "pm.test('At least one CodeSystem is loaded', () => entries.length > 0);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}/api/terminology/fhir/CodeSystem?_summary=true",
          "host": [
            "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "terminology",
            "fhir",
            "CodeSystem"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "_summary",
              "value": "true"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "3c. Terminology - List loaded ValueSets (binding coverage)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const b = pm.response.json();",
              "const entries = b.entry || [];",
              "console.log('Loaded ValueSets (' + entries.length + '):');",
              "entries.forEach(e => { const vs = e.resource || {}; console.log(`  id=${vs.id}  url=${vs.url}  version=${vs.version}`); });",
              "console.log('For an inactive code to surface during bundle validation, the ValueSet the target element BINDS to must appear here, and your inactive code must be a MEMBER of it.');",
              "pm.test('At least one ValueSet is loaded (else valueset binding checks fall back to in-memory)', () => entries.length > 0);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}/api/terminology/fhir/ValueSet?_summary=true",
          "host": [
            "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "terminology",
            "fhir",
            "ValueSet"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "_summary",
              "value": "true"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Terminology - Confirm code is INACTIVE",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Code found', () => pm.response.code === 200);",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "console.log('Code status:', JSON.stringify(body));",
              "pm.test('Code status is Inactive', () => /inactive/i.test(JSON.stringify(body)));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}/api/terminology/config/code-systems/{{codeSystemId}}/codes/{{code}}",
          "host": [
            "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "terminology",
            "config",
            "code-systems",
            "{{codeSystemId}}",
            "codes",
            "{{code}}"
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Terminology - $validate-code (expect inactive issue)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const p = pm.response.json();",
              "console.log('$validate-code response:', JSON.stringify(p, null, 2));",
              "const params = p.parameter || [];",
              "const result = params.find(x => x.name === 'result');",
              "pm.test('result = true (valid but inactive)', () => result && result.valueBoolean === true);",
              "const issues = params.find(x => x.name === 'issues');",
              "pm.test('issues OperationOutcome carries an inactive warning', () => {",
              "  const txt = JSON.stringify(issues || {});",
              "  return /inactive/i.test(txt);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/fhir+json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"resourceType\": \"Parameters\",\n  \"parameter\": [\n    { \"name\": \"url\", \"valueUri\": \"{{codeSystem}}\" },\n    { \"name\": \"code\", \"valueString\": \"{{code}}\" }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}/api/terminology/fhir/CodeSystem/$validate-code",
          "host": [
            "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "terminology",
            "fhir",
            "CodeSystem",
            "$validate-code"
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "5b. Terminology - $validate-code against ValueSet (binding proxy)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// This is exactly the call HAPI makes for the element's binding. If result=true AND inactive,",
              "// step 9 will surface the inactive warning; if result=false, the code is NOT a member of the valueset.",
              "const p = pm.response.json();",
              "console.log('ValueSet $validate-code response:', JSON.stringify(p, null, 2));",
              "const params = p.parameter || [];",
              "const result = params.find(x => x.name === 'result');",
              "pm.test('code is a MEMBER of the binding valueset (result=true)', () => result && result.valueBoolean === true);",
              "const issues = params.find(x => x.name === 'issues');",
              "pm.test('inactive issue present at the valueset level', () => /inactive/i.test(JSON.stringify(issues || {})));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/fhir+json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"resourceType\": \"Parameters\",\n  \"parameter\": [\n    { \"name\": \"url\", \"valueUri\": \"{{bindingValueSetUrl}}\" },\n    { \"name\": \"system\", \"valueUri\": \"{{codeSystem}}\" },\n    { \"name\": \"code\", \"valueString\": \"{{code}}\" }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}/api/terminology/fhir/ValueSet/$validate-code",
          "host": [
            "{{terminologyBaseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "terminology",
            "fhir",
            "ValueSet",
            "$validate-code"
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Validation - Initialize Artifacts (profiles)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Artifacts initialized', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 202, 204]));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{validationBaseUrl}}/api/validation/artifact/$initialize",
          "host": [
            "{{validationBaseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "validation",
            "artifact",
            "$initialize"
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "7. Validation - Initialize Categories",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Categories initialized', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 202, 204]));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{validationBaseUrl}}/api/validation/category/$initialize",
          "host": [
            "{{validationBaseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "validation",
            "category",
            "$initialize"
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "8. Validation - Confirm inactive category loaded",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Expected inactive category exists', () => pm.response.code === 200);",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) { console.log('Category:', JSON.stringify(pm.response.json())); }"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{validationBaseUrl}}/api/validation/category/{{expectedCategoryId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{validationBaseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "validation",
            "category",
            "{{expectedCategoryId}}"
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "9. Validation - $validate?categorize=true (THE TEST)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Validate returned 200', () => pm.response.code === 200);",
              "const results = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('Response is a results array', () => Array.isArray(results));",
              "",
              "// Find the inactive-code result (surfacing check)",
              "const inactive = (results || []).find(r => /has a status of inactive/i.test(r.message || ''));",
              "if (inactive) {",
              "  console.log('INACTIVE RESULT:', JSON.stringify(inactive, null, 2));",
              "} else {",
              "  console.log('No inactive result. All messages:');",
              "  (results || []).forEach(r => console.log(`[${r.severity}] expr=${r.expression} | ${r.message}`));",
              "}",
              "pm.test('SURFACING: inactive warning is present as a Result', () => !!inactive);",
              "",
              "// Categorization check",
              "if (inactive) {",
              "  const cats = (inactive.categories || []).map(c => c.id);",
              "  console.log('Categories on inactive result:', cats.join(', '));",
              "  pm.test('CATEGORIZED as a missing_active_* category', () => cats.some(id => /^missing_active_/.test(id)));",
              "  pm.test(`CATEGORIZED as ${pm.collectionVariables.get('expectedCategoryId')}`, () => cats.includes(pm.collectionVariables.get('expectedCategoryId')));",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {},
            "requests": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/fhir+json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"resourceType\": \"Bundle\",\n  \"type\": \"collection\",\n  \"entry\": [\n    {\n      \"fullUrl\": \"urn:uuid:enc-1\",\n      \"resource\": {\n        \"resourceType\": \"Encounter\",\n        \"id\": \"enc-1\",\n        \"meta\": { \"profile\": [\"{{profileUrl}}\"] },\n        \"identifier\": [ { \"system\": \"urn:example\", \"value\": \"enc-1\" } ],\n        \"status\": \"finished\",\n        \"class\": { \"system\": \"http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ActCode\", \"code\": \"SS\", \"display\": \"short stay\" },\n        \"type\": [ { \"coding\": [ { \"system\": \"{{codeSystem}}\", \"code\": \"{{code}}\", \"display\": \"{{codeDisplay}}\" } ] } ],\n        \"subject\": { \"reference\": \"Patient/pat-1\" }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"fullUrl\": \"Patient/pat-1\",\n      \"resource\": {\n        \"resourceType\": \"Patient\",\n        \"id\": \"pat-1\",\n        \"extension\": [\n          {\n            \"url\": \"http://hl7.org/fhir/us/core/StructureDefinition/us-core-race\",\n            \"extension\": [\n              { \"url\": \"ombCategory\", \"valueCoding\": { \"system\": \"urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.6.238\", \"code\": \"1002-5\", \"display\": \"American Indian or Alaska Native\" } },\n              { \"url\": \"detailed\", \"valueCoding\": { \"system\": \"urn:oid:2.16.840.1.113883.6.238\", \"code\": \"1004-1\", \"display\": \"American Indian\" } },\n              { \"url\": \"text\", \"valueString\": \"American Indian\" }\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{validationBaseUrl}}/api/validation/$validate?categorize=true",
          "host": [
            "{{validationBaseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "validation",
            "$validate"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "categorize",
              "value": "true"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "packages": {},
        "requests": {},
        "exec": [
